WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:05.790
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and there are
just so many WTF moments in this week’s

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.960
Walking Dead, we need to get right in it.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:13.680
A whole bunch of plots were tied up and there
was a major homage to a comic book moment.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.881
Quick shout out for the giveaway this week.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.240
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m doing a weekly Walking Dead giveaway,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:22.259
just to say thank you to you guys for being
so awesome.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:29.869
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:33.650
We have some major stuff to work out here,
so I’m going to do my Top 5 WTF moments,

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:34.870
then my review.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:37.210
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.260
Here we go,

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.070
Number 5 - Lizzie’s New Friend Grizelda.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.520
There was so much wrong about this, did anyone
else scream at their tv?

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.170
Her performance, the actress was a little
too much, but we got the message.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.370
Lizzie is batshit crazy.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:57.210
The best part was seeing Carol get that look
on her face like, I’m so going to end up

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.330
having to put Lizzie down.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.900
And then the camera pans over to Tyreese looking
through the window and he’s got the ‘what

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.160
the fuuuu’ face.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:10.190
It’s pretty clear even at this point that
Lizzie is going to be the biggest problem

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.190
in this episode.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:16.600
Not Walkers, not finding food, not Mika toughening
up and not finding the others.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.380
Number 4 - Lizzie feeds the Walker.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.380
What the eff.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.980
At least we finally got a definitive answer
about who was feeding the Walkers.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.530
This was so disturbing.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.710
Lizzie shall make you understand.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.220
Based on the scenes in the teaser I knew that
she wasn’t going to get bitten this soon

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.520
in the episode, but the minute her hand reached
out I just wanted to slap her.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.990
It seems like in her mind she’s seeing all
of them as they were and just can’t move

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:39.990
forward in her mind.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:43.380
Developmentally she’s just stuck at the
point of the outbreak before everything went

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.380
to hell.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.380
I did love how Mika just walked up to Lizzie
and the walker like it was no big deal.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.020
You’d think if there was a walker nearby
you’d do everything you

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.760
Number 3 - Tyreese remembers Karen.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.390
The irony of the scene was just beautiful
with Carol in the foreground and Tyreese just

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.660
going on and on about his Karen Nightmares.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.340
Remember earlier in the episode where he’s
asleep on the chair jerking around.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.479
He was probably having a Karen Nightmare right
then.

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:08.869
I really did expect Carol to come clean when
she goes to speak, but I’m glad she saved

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:10.320
it for later in the episode.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.540
Did anyone else laugh a little bit when Tyreese
went to hug her and had the gun in his hand

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.730
as he wrapped it around Carol.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.060
It’s like they were saying, murder is right
around the corner.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.250
Which is why the next moment was so appropriate.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.440
Number 2 - Lizzie kills Mika.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.240
She’s full on Ben.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.840
I was just about to change Judith too.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.390
Everyone had been wondering if they girls
were going to take the place of Ben and Billy.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.540
And it went down exactly the way it did in
the comics.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.860
Here’s a shot of Ben right after killing
his brother.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:43.569
The only difference is that Carl was involved
in the resolution and in the episode it’s

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:44.569
Carol.

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:48.140
After seeing Lizzie’s character progression
this season, and this episode, I don’t think

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.620
there’s any other way this could have gone
down.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.069
Even if they had made it to Terminus together,
Lizzie still would have continued doing the

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:57.830
same things and because Mika was so attached
to her, she would have either been killed

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.500
by a Walker because of Lizzie or by Lizzie
herself.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:07.880
So unless Lizzie turned first, Mika would
have died eventually no matter what.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.110
Number 1 - Carol kills Lizzie.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.220
Just look at the flowers and count 1.2.3.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:19.430
Because I’d read the comic story I kept
expecting this to happen since the Mika killing

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.640
was exactly like the twin killing in the comics.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.970
I think they made it a little more emotional
since Carol was like they’re surrogate Mother.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.190
I had actually expected her to shoot Lizzie
on the spot when she got the gun out of her

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.190
hand.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:38.140
I wasn’t a huge fan of the transition from
Mika to the house to Carol shooting Lizzie.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.410
The pace just felt a little stop and go.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:43.190
And I had hoped that Lizzie’s death would
have been a little more intense.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.989
There was a lot they chose not to show us
in the episode.

00:03:45.989 --> 00:03:50.570
They didn’t show Lizzie stabbing Mika and
they didn’t show the bullet hitting Lizzie’s

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:51.570
head.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:56.290
Personally I think they shot it that way and
AMC made them take it out.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.739
But you can comment on whether or not you
think they intended to show us the actual

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.739
deaths.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.610
In the end, I’m glad she’s dead.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.400
If you didn’t hate Lizzie before this episode,
then this was the last straw.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.690
I have no idea where they would have gone
with her character had she lived and made

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.690
it to terminus.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:19.500
Clearly she was going to kill Baby Judith,
after she confessed as much I wanted Carol

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.410
to shoot her so bad.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:26.250
And my bonus WTF moment - Carol Confesses
To Tyreese.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.090
I love how you can see murder on his face
as he’s just shaking the table with his

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.090
grip.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.520
But he’s wrapping his brain around it and
forgives her.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.680
Not to say that he’ll ever forget.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.980
I love his quote though.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.280
“It’s a part of you now.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.280
Me too.”

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.340
It’s a big callback to Tyreese’s earlier
talk with Carol about the talking to them.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.800
And Carol’s answer that they’re not haunting
them, just reminding them of what they have

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
to do.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.800
And so they continue on to terminus.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.860
I think we’re meant to take away that Tyreese
isn’t going to harm Carol, but they’re

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.490
never going to be pals they way they might
have been, had awful things not happened.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.120
Tyreese wanted to stay at the cottage so bad.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:05.669
How ironic that he said he wasn’t ready
to be around people when Carol then said Lizzie

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:08.220
can’t be around other people.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.090
Let it not go unsaid though, the thing I was
most excited about in this episode was Baby

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.350
Judith NOT dying.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:17.150
As awful as everything was, that made me happy.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.500
But now it’s your turn, what was your biggest
WTF moment?

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.770
The deaths, or some of the craziness that
preceded them.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.770
Each Lizzie moment throughout the episode
felt like it successively increase my stress

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.460
levels.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.140
Overall I give the episode an A for having
the guts, so to speak, to kill of two major

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:40.460
characters in a way completely faithful to
the comics.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.550
As an asterisk though, I give Lizzie’s performance
a C for acting.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:48.820
I knew what the actress was trying to convey,
she’s like the Joffrey of the episode.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:52.620
And the problem with that is that they’re
supposed to make you hate them, which they

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.620
do beautifully.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.250
But when you hate a character, sometimes they’re
unbearable to watch.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.560
Mika’s performance was a fresh breath of
sanity.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.729
Mika get your gun.

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:04.949
I would have liked to see the deleted scene
that preceded her stabbing, maybe it will

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:06.990
be on the DVD.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:11.240
But I don’t think even HBO would show a
child stabbing another child.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.850
Even on Game of Thrones when Arya killed that
boy in season 1, they kind of cut away really

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.850
quickly.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:20.800
I’ll say the child acting I did love in
the episode was when Mika was comforting Lizzie

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.040
the first time and they chant in unison.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.790
It reminded me of the creepy twin girls from
The Shining.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:27.460
Did anyone else get that vibe?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.520
I loved Tyree’s performance in the episode.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:35.580
I almost felt like he had the hardest job.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.830
He had to convey all these emotions without
really doing anything.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.540
His character is not a good communicator,
so a lot of his performance has to be physical.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.740
And that last scene with Carol was beautifully
intense.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:50.180
Let me know what you thought of the episode,
and are you happy Lizzie is dead.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.169
Even if it meant Mika had to die too.

